a module. Could set module_designation: \"Indicating device\"? Hmm, that's about the certified module. For a complete water meter, module might be \"Not applicable\". Not clearly stated. I'll omit module_designation. Actually, the fragment mentions indicating device characteristics — that's part of the meter. I'll leave module_designation out or null. Omit.\n\nShould I include a description? Not really present. Omit.\n\n**manufacturers[]**: production location — \"The water meter is produced at one of the following production locations: Badger Meter Czech Republic s.r.o., Maříkova 2082/26, 621 00 Brno, Czech Republic\". Include as manufacturer entry. It's labeled \"Production location\" not \"Manufacturer\" — but in OIML certs production locations are manufacturers. I'll include it under manufacturers with name and address_lines.\n\nNow, model_family models: Should model_id be \"DN50\" etc.? Yes.\n\nAlso note Table 4's footnote applies to DN600 indicating range — in model_level, footnote_markers: [\"*\"].\n\nLet me now also consider whether to include \"characteristics.config_level\": not applicable. Omit.\n\nNumber normalization check:\n- \"99.999\" → 99999 (Dutch thousands). Yes.\n- \"999.999\" → 999999\n- \"9.999.999\" → 9999999\n- \"99.999.999*\" → 99999999\n- \"0,0001\" → 0.0001\n- \"0,001\" → 0.001\n- \"0,01\" → 0.01\n- \"0,1\" → 0.1\n\nGood.\n\nDates in revision history: convert to ISO: \"2021-01-11\", \"2022-03-17\", \"2023-06-15\", \"2023-07-04\", \"2024-05-17\", \"2025-04-17\", \"2025-07-31\", \"2025-10-03\".\n\nRevision \"Initial\" → revision: \"Initial\". changes: null.\n\nRevision 7 changes text: \"Addition of new electronics housing and external battery version. Addition software version 2.0.62\" (merging the <br> lines).\n\nNow assemble JSON:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-NL1-21.03\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"project_number\": \"3954718\",\n    \"page_total\": 7,\n    \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\",\n  